{
  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "The most important open question is why adding the image modality in the multiprofile setting hurts performance (config_030: 0.632 vs. config_005/006: 0.650/0.653), despite helping in the singleprofile setting (config_028: 0.536 vs. config_004: 0.520). Since image-only performance is very weak (0.208), the image features likely introduce noise that concat fusion passes through undiluted. Config_031 is a single-variable change from config_030 (concat → weighted fusion), directly testing whether learned fusion weights can downweight the noisy image signal and restore/exceed the RNA-only multiprofile baseline. This is the most efficient next experiment: if weighted fusion recovers performance, it identifies fusion as the bottleneck and opens a path to a superior multimodal configuration; if it does not, it confirms the image modality is fundamentally incompatible with strong RNA multiprofile signal, saving future budget from further multimodal-multiprofile exploration. No other single experiment resolves this key design uncertainty as cleanly."
}

